When the public exponent e = 3 (a very small value) and the message m is relatively short, we have:

    m³ < N

  Because m³ is smaller than the modulus N, the modulo reduction has no effect:

    c ≡ m³ pmod N implies c = m³

  To decrypt, we simply need to calculate the integer cube root of c without needing to factor N or know the private key d!
